                                 Mover History
                                 -------------

(Newest at the top)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

2/5/93
1.6   Bug Fix release - Mover was incorrectly calculating dates.  It believed
         that a file date 2/1/93 was older than a file dated 1/31/93.  Fixed.
      Added Mover.guide to distribution.  You will need AmigaGuide or an AG
         viewer to be able to use it.

1/12/93
1.5   Added support for moving files to/from the HOLD directory
       o HOLD directory now shows up as another directory to choose from
       o Automatically removes '/' from description
       o offers to increase uploaders byte/file count
       o Knows where the HOLD directory is

      Fixed an incompatibility with text editors that strip trailing
         whitespace (AZ)
       o Mover will now correctly deal with "blank" description lines created
            when an editors strips a line of spaces.

      Improved file handling
       o Mover will not duplicate "Sent By" lines any more

      Found a message being created internally but not being sent out.

(I forget)
1.4   Added support back in for editting descriptions
       o AmiExpress's editor does not properly limit the number of characters
            that can be entered on a line.  Also, the editor really, really
            barks.  However, I believe the sysop now has the option of
            changing the default editor, so some people may be better off.
            Perhaps soon Joe will add support for door editors in message
            bases so I can release my full-screen editor!

      Added support for Sysop uploads
       o Sysop can choose directory and file patterns for moving files and
            creating descriptions.

      Added support for creating/modifying MOVER.CFG files on the fly
       o Now no one has to know how to do it!

      Added support for decreasing a users byte count when deleting a file


(I forgot)
1.3   Bug fixes probably!  History log began with version 1.5, and I don't
         feel like dragging this stuff out of the RCS.